+/**
+ * @brief Reset the GATT server to its initial state.
+ *
+ * This function clears all registered services, characteristics and
+ * descriptors, and releases any memory allocated for client‑configuration
+ * handling.  After a successful reset the host behaves as if it has never
+ * had any GATT services registered – callers may queue new services with
+ * @ref ble_gatts_add_svcs and then start the server again with
+ * @ref ble_gatts_start.
+ *
+ * The reset may only be performed when the host is idle – i.e. no active
+ * connections exist and no GAP procedures (advertising, scanning or a
